{"data": [{"author_id": "1659439170883026945", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:28:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117413541548614094"], "id": "2117413541548614094", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid Tool descriptions are where the context goes. Back in February Slack's official MCP integration took 16K tokens just by being enabled, and when I audited our own MCP descriptions after that, I cut them by 60% and everything still worked.", "url": "https://x.com/jackrudenko/status/2117413541548614094"}, {"author_id": "847599342630260736", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:46:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117403002751557720"], "id": "2117403002751557720", "in_reply_to_user_id": "713450451446968321", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117292668698939881", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@JohnDinsdale48 @_philschmid no because\n1. the performance of the script execution itself is negligible compared to the tools it's calling\n2. compile time would dwarf any runtime benefit\n3. rust doesnt protect from agent writing malicious code. what you need here is sandboxed execution/interpretation", "url": "https://x.com/fu5ha/status/2117403002751557720"}, {"author_id": "1345374773916921856", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:30:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117399001888677951"], "id": "2117399001888677951", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "1978624380155441228", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid https://t.co/K4fNEvltMU https://t.co/tafbwKHRtV", "url": "https://x.com/AtakanTekparmak/status/2117399001888677951"}, {"author_id": "2043889585399443462", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:17:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117395593320403423"], "id": "2117395593320403423", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid Code mode makes sense to me since models have read far more code than tool schemas. The typed sandbox is the part I'd want, because a type error is a much clearer failure than a bash command that half works.", "url": "https://x.com/Johnqyph/status/2117395593320403423"}, {"author_id": "130821141", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:01:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117391675299663999"], "id": "2117391675299663999", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid One tool helps the model and hurts the audit. If the trace only says 'ran code', nobody can show later what the agent touched or on whose behalf. Our first AI service desk discarded which sources backed each answer. Code mode must log every call made inside the sandbox.", "url": "https://x.com/luizhmcarvalho/status/2117391675299663999"}, {"author_id": "1889019962", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:22:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117381945797550317"], "id": "2117381945797550317", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid curious how you handle a script failing midway in code mode. with plain tool calls each failure comes back as one result, with a 10-call script dying at call 7 the agent first has to work out what already ran", "url": "https://x.com/alishohadaee/status/2117381945797550317"}, {"author_id": "1592549190470598657", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:21:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117381532004307427"], "id": "2117381532004307427", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 86, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid Great article.\nAlso this feels basically like what Codex already does, writing long-ass Powershell commands with inlined python to do whatever it wants!", "url": "https://x.com/packers_owner_j/status/2117381532004307427"}, {"author_id": "780117123544682496", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:12:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117379306888241266"], "id": "2117379306888241266", "in_reply_to_user_id": "103844545", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117370983606567359", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Shashikant86 @_philschmid dynamic tool search was the hack. writing typed code is just programming", "url": "https://x.com/ElenaAIArt/status/2117379306888241266"}, {"author_id": "864133566", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:11:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117379202743943493"], "id": "2117379202743943493", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid Because @badlogicgames said so!", "url": "https://x.com/leiserfg/status/2117379202743943493"}, {"author_id": "780117123544682496", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:10:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117378777219219626"], "id": "2117378777219219626", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1791316096076722176", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117336453416108294", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AyushManiar @_philschmid my guess is it improves. with bash the model reasons in shell syntax, typed python lets it chain and parallelize directly. someone should rerun the benchmark 👀", "url": "https://x.com/ElenaAIArt/status/2117378777219219626"}, {"author_id": "780117123544682496", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:07:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117378133531738120"], "id": "2117378133531738120", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1121764238593273857", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117364997730738280", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@pachu2120 @_philschmid fair critique. the mixed bag point is real, half the MCP servers i've wired up have schemas that fall apart on contact. but the token math still favors code mode for chatty loops, way fewer round trips per task", "url": "https://x.com/ElenaAIArt/status/2117378133531738120"}, {"author_id": "780117123544682496", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:05:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117377478016802818"], "id": "2117377478016802818", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid typed sandbox over bash makes sense to me. bash falls apart the moment you need state between steps. code mode is just admitting the model was writing a program all along", "url": "https://x.com/ElenaAIArt/status/2117377478016802818"}, {"author_id": "103844545", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:39:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117370983606567359"], "id": "2117370983606567359", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 103, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid Agent already has one tool and it seems working Pretty well in the Prime Agent self impropE harness. \n\nCode mode is really technology of last year which bets too much on tool search and entice sandboxers like Cloudflare and others. Recently  one to know that it sucks on tool", "url": "https://x.com/Shashikant86/status/2117370983606567359"}, {"author_id": "1121764238593273857", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:15:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117364997730738280"], "id": "2117364997730738280", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 157, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid idk the arguments of this vs bash is pretty weak I think:\n\n1. Typed functions - Your 3p tools are going to be a mix of MCP &amp; CLI. The actual typed schemas you will get here will be a mixed bag at best.\n\n2. Like I mentioned, the tools will be a mixed bag, your gonna have to do", "url": "https://x.com/pachu2120/status/2117364997730738280"}, {"author_id": "1981091420082442240", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:59:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117361062626337074"], "id": "2117361062626337074", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid So part of my sandbox strategy is that an agent builds an environment and a cli within that container for agents to interact with.  (We manage the network of the containers and the AI has no ability to change that.) \n\nTo accomplish that, tools on the host need to be managed", "url": "https://x.com/MaybushSha16067/status/2117361062626337074"}, {"author_id": "2057821997141245953", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:38:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117355608441598292"], "id": "2117355608441598292", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid Does the every action inside exec still get independent authorization and logging? \n\nI don't think I would blindly trust this without another security-aware model noting its safety.", "url": "https://x.com/cachetronaut_/status/2117355608441598292"}, {"author_id": "85792897", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:20:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117351086298116312"], "id": "2117351086298116312", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 134, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid would this work on weak models though?", "url": "https://x.com/xesgarcia/status/2117351086298116312"}, {"author_id": "1267062923073073158", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:14:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117349677079437654"], "id": "2117349677079437654", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 32, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid @badlogicgames", "url": "https://x.com/joaomviso/status/2117349677079437654"}, {"author_id": "15503374", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:06:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117347593592123513"], "id": "2117347593592123513", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 145, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid Hm, interesting. With native tool search everywhere, code mode feels sooo last year technology.", "url": "https://x.com/chaliy/status/2117347593592123513"}, {"author_id": "1828410741063348224", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:40:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117341109873524964"], "id": "2117341109873524964", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid the typed sandbox needs types from somewhere, and mcp schemas are already sitting there. so code mode probably doesn't kill mcp, it just turns it from the tool list into the import list. which is kind of a better job for it anyway", "url": "https://x.com/jj_kovacs/status/2117341109873524964"}, {"author_id": "1791316096076722176", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:22:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117336453416108294"], "id": "2117336453416108294", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 154, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid @_philschmid Love this article !!\n\nHave you taken a look at the Harness Zero research paper ? (https://t.co/VKaCKfLRmq)\n\nI am wondering how this paper would look like with code_mode as the ```execute tool``` call (as opposed to Bash as the exec tool call)", "url": "https://x.com/AyushManiar/status/2117336453416108294"}, {"author_id": "854669606249693184", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:46:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117327500208754778"], "id": "2117327500208754778", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 40, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid typed sandbox &gt; raw bash once the agent starts touching prod", "url": "https://x.com/SamuraiPhonk/status/2117327500208754778"}, {"author_id": "2084142065307533313", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:40:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117325960001515688"], "id": "2117325960001515688", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid The sandbox constraint is the key tradeoff. Typed execution gives you safety and introspection at the cost of needing bridges back to the host environment, which is where MCP becomes useful again once the code interpreter needs to read files or call services.", "url": "https://x.com/BoboLinNotes/status/2117325960001515688"}, {"author_id": "79401622", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:24:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117321919884112311"], "id": "2117321919884112311", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 52, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid Code mode like behaviour is essential for sandbox agents that do not have full cli access (like agents on the phone) to be efficient with context and get composition on tool calls.", "url": "https://x.com/slaser79/status/2117321919884112311"}, {"author_id": "2071719264000552960", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:14:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117319387527127169"], "id": "2117319387527127169", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid the typed sandbox is the part that matters, not the collapsing. one tool that runs code still hands the agent a shell in disguise unless the call is checked against a schema before it runs. bash takes a string, a typed call has a shape you can refuse.", "url": "https://x.com/cyberogz/status/2117319387527127169"}], "includes": {"tweets": [{"author_id": "1141052916570214400", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:30:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117278154918092817"], "id": "2117278154918092817", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 189, "impression_count": 16231, "like_count": 267, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 56, "retweet_count": 18}, "text": "Are Agents soon going to have only 1 tool? We went from a handful of tools, to dynamic tool search, and now to collapsing everything into code mode. \n\nWrote down how Code Mode works, why a typed JS/Python sandbox can beat raw bash, and why MCP is going to go back strong in 2027. https://t.co/Po9WhVEZ1h"}, {"author_id": "713450451446968321", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:28:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117292668698939881"], "id": "2117292668698939881", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 377, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid Should that be a Rust sandbox for safety nad performance?"}, {"author_id": "1345374773916921856", "created_at": "2025-10-16T00:49:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["1978624380155441228"], "id": "1978624380155441228", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 703, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "1978469122666086905", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Told yall https://t.co/MvfHsu6De4 https://t.co/Ru5bybZuZ9"}, {"author_id": "103844545", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:39:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117370983606567359"], "id": "2117370983606567359", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 103, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid Agent already has one tool and it seems working Pretty well in the Prime Agent self impropE harness. \n\nCode mode is really technology of last year which bets too much on tool search and entice sandboxers like Cloudflare and others. Recently  one to know that it sucks on tool"}, {"author_id": "1791316096076722176", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:22:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117336453416108294"], "id": "2117336453416108294", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 154, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid @_philschmid Love this article !!\n\nHave you taken a look at the Harness Zero research paper ? (https://t.co/VKaCKfLRmq)\n\nI am wondering how this paper would look like with code_mode as the ```execute tool``` call (as opposed to Bash as the exec tool call)"}, {"author_id": "1121764238593273857", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:15:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117364997730738280"], "id": "2117364997730738280", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1141052916570214400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 157, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117278154918092817", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_philschmid idk the arguments of this vs bash is pretty weak I think:\n\n1. Typed functions - Your 3p tools are going to be a mix of MCP &amp; CLI. The actual typed schemas you will get here will be a mixed bag at best.\n\n2. Like I mentioned, the tools will be a mixed bag, your gonna have to do"}], "users": [{"id": "1659439170883026945", "name": "Jack Rudenko", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 196, "following_count": 673, "like_count": 1663, "listed_count": 2, "media_count": 379, "tweet_count": 1891}, "username": "jackrudenko"}, {"id": "847599342630260736", "name": "gray 🌄", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 2731, "following_count": 1187, "like_count": 63879, "listed_count": 51, "media_count": 1675, "tweet_count": 22351}, "username": "fu5ha"}, {"id": "1345374773916921856", "name": "Atakan Tekparmak", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 1126, "following_count": 1559, "like_count": 99298, "listed_count": 25, "media_count": 301, "tweet_count": 4278}, "username": "AtakanTekparmak"}, {"id": "2043889585399443462", "name": "John", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 0, "following_count": 34, "like_count": 30, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 0, "tweet_count": 28}, "username": "Johnqyph"}, {"id": "130821141", "name": "Luiz Carvalho", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 33, "following_count": 144, "like_count": 23, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 5, "tweet_count": 58}, "username